course: dictionary
lesson: 1761
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word clear can mean different things, so the words around it tell you which meaning is right. «A clear family rule about buying prevents most arguments.» Here clear means easy to understand, so everyone knows what the rule is.
explain: «Blowing too hard makes a recorder jump up to a shrill squeal; a soft, steady breath gives a clear note.» A clear note is easy to hear and sounds clean, with no fuzzy or breathy sound. Ask yourself: which meaning of clear fits here?
explain: Clear can also be a doing word. «Please clear the table» means take the things off it. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: Clear has many meanings, so context tells you which one to use.
fact: Clear can mean easy to understand, as in «clear instructions».
fact: Clear can mean see-through, like clean water or glass. These are transparent, so light can pass through them.
fact: Clear can mean with no cloud or rain, as in «a clear sky», or with nothing in the way, as in «a clear road».
fact: Clear can be a verb: «clear the table» means remove things, and «it cleared up» means the weather became bright. Stay clear of something means keep away from it.
exercise: «Keep clear of the edge of the platform.» What does clear mean here? | *Stay away from | Easy to read | Bright and sunny | Wipe clean with a cloth
exercise: Tom says, «The water in the pond is clear.» What does clear mean? | It is easy to understand | It has been cleared away | *You can see through it | It has no clouds in it
exercise: «It cleared up after the storm, and the sky turned blue.» What does cleared up mean here? | The sky was emptied of clouds and rain | *The weather became bright | The storm made a loud noise | Someone tidied the sky
test: «The teacher gave clear instructions, so everyone knew what to do.» What does clear mean? | Without clouds | *Easy to understand | Made of glass | Cleared away
test: «Please clear the table before the guests arrive.» What does clear mean? | Keep away from the table | Make the table bright | Wipe the table with a cloth | *Remove things from the table
exam: «The rules were clear before the race began, so nobody could argue.» What does clear mean? | Without any cloud | Made of glass | *Easy to understand, with no doubt | Far away from the start
